#lang ivy1.8

# ===========================================================================
# MOESI cache coherence protocol -- LIVENESS (arbitrary arbiter)
#
#   "every memory access issued by a cache is eventually served"
#
#       forall C. globally ( waiting(C) -> eventually ~waiting(C) )
#
# under weak fairness (justice) for every rule of the protocol, PLUS
# compassion (strong fairness) for the home's request arbiter.
#
# The model is `moesi.ivy` (read that file first for the protocol itself),
# plus four additions:
#
#   1. `finite type client`  -- a fixed but arbitrary number of caches.  This
#      is what makes `work_created = true` a legitimate finite bound R
#      (Rule 5 of McMillan, CAV'24).
#   2. a ghost bit `waiting(C)`, raised when C issues a request and lowered
#      when C consumes the corresponding grant.  `~waiting(C)` is exactly
#      "the access completed".  Clients block while waiting, so at most one
#      request per cache is in flight and the obligation is well posed.
#   3. weak-fairness instrumentation: every rule gets a flag pulsed
#      *before* its guard is tested, and the rule becomes a guarded command.
#      `globally eventually wf_x` then says "the scheduler offers rule x a
#      turn infinitely often", which is a statement about the scheduler and
#      not about the protocol -- see LIVENESS_CASE_STUDY_GERMAN.md section 3.
#   4. a compassion (strong fairness) assumption for the request arbiter.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY COMPASSION
#
# `pickNewRequestRule(cl)` picks an *arbitrary* client with a pending request.
# Under weak fairness the scheduler must offer client _C's pick a turn
# infinitely often, but it may offer every one of those turns while the home
# is busy serving somebody else: other caches cycle request -> service ->
# request forever, the home is idle only in the instants between a grant and
# the next pick, and the adversary simply never schedules _C's turn in one of
# those instants.  The property is *false* under weak fairness alone.  This is
# not an artefact of the encoding; it is a property of an arbiter that does
# not remember who is waiting.  So we assume compassion, and only for the
# arbiter -- every other rule has a guard that is stable once enabled.
#
# `moesi_live.ivy` proves the *incomparable* theorem for a MOESI home with a
# FIFO arbiter, where weak fairness alone suffices.  Neither result implies
# the other.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE THREE STAGES
#
# A waiting client is in exactly one of
#
#   stage 1   channel1(C) ~= empty1                       request queued
#   stage 2   homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & hcc = C      the home is serving C
#   stage 3   channel2_4(C) = grant{shared,exclusive,modified}   grant in flight
#
# (invariant [waiting_stages]; [stage1_excl] / [stage2_excl] make them
# disjoint).  This is what discharges the "something is always scheduled"
# premise S4 of the ranking rule.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE LEXICOGRAPHIC RANKING  (Rule 10 / 11; tactic `ranking`)
#
#   [00][01]     stage 1: the two tableau cases of the compassion antecedent
#                                                               (highest)
#   [02][03][04] stage 3: _C consumes its grant (one per grant kind)
#   [05][06][07] stage 2: the invalidation pipeline  (write requests)
#   [08][09][10] stage 2: the downgrade pipeline     (read requests, M/E hit)
#   [11][12][13] stage 2: draining a stale grant that blocks a probe
#   [14][15][16] stage 2: the home issues the grant, ending the command
#                                                               (lowest)
#
# Why it has to be lexicographic and not Rule 8 (`l2s_auto5`): while _C sits
# in stage 1 or stage 3, the home runs *whole commands for other clients*,
# and those grow every pipeline ranking ([05] grows when a grant adds a
# sharer, [14] grows when a pick makes the home busy).  Rule 8 requires every
# ranking to be conserved by every action, so it would need the pipeline to
# be lifted into a separate lemma.  Rule 10 lets a *preempted* component --
# one for which a higher-order scheduler is on -- grow.  The load-bearing
# fact is
#
#     ~pre([05]..[16])  /\  waiting(_C)
#       ==>  stage 2,  or  ( stage 1  and  ~(eventually E) )
#
# and both of those imply homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1: if no stage-1 or
# stage-3 scheduler is on and _C is waiting, then either the home is serving
# _C, or _C's request is queued while ~(eventually E) says the home is never
# idle again.  A busy home cannot pick, so nothing grows the pipeline in the
# non-preempted region.  That is why every pipeline ranking carries a "the
# home is busy" conjunct.
#
# Two `ranking`-tactic facts worth knowing (see LIVENESS_CASE_STUDY_GERMAN.md
# section 6): only `l2s_needed_preserved` and `l2s_sched_stable` get the
# preemption discount -- `l2s_progress` does not, so every scheduler below is
# literally the enabling guard of its rule.  And component suffixes are
# sorted as *strings*, hence two digits.
# ===========================================================================

# A fixed, but arbitrary, number of caches.  Finiteness is what makes the
# relational rankings below finite (Rule 5).
finite type client

type message1    = { empty1 , reqshared , reqexclusive }
type message2_4  = { empty2_4 , invalidate , downgrade ,
                     grantshared , grantexclusive , grantmodified }
type message3    = { empty3 , invalidateAck , downgradeAck }
type cachestate  = { invalid , shared , owned , exclusive , modified }

object s = {
    var channel1(C:client)   : message1
    var channel2_4(C:client) : message2_4
    var channel3(C:client)   : message3
    var cache(C:client)      : cachestate

    var homeSharerList(C:client)  : bool
    var homeprobeList(C:client)   : bool
    var homeexclusiveGranted      : bool
    var homeCurrentCommand        : message1
    var homeCurrentclient         : client

    # Ghost: "C has an outstanding access".  Raised at the request, lowered
    # when the grant is consumed.  The liveness property is about this bit.
    var waiting(C:client) : bool
}

var owner : client       # the cache holding the line writable, or owning it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Weak-fairness (justice) flags: one per rule, pulsed unconditionally before
# the guard, so the rule is always callable and a turn on a disabled rule is
# a stutter step.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var wf_pick(C:client)        : bool      # pickNewRequestRule: turn offered
var f_pick(C:client)         : bool      # pickNewRequestRule: actually fired
var wf_sendinv(C:client)     : bool      # sendinvalidateRule
var wf_senddown(C:client)    : bool      # senddowngradeRule
var wf_clientinv(C:client)   : bool      # clientinvalidatesRule
var wf_clientdown(C:client)  : bool      # clientdowngradesRule
var wf_recvinvack(C:client)  : bool      # receiveinvalidateAckRule
var wf_recvdownack(C:client) : bool      # receivedowngradeAckRule
var wf_recvshared(C:client)  : bool      # receivesharedGrantRule
var wf_recvexcl(C:client)    : bool      # receiveexclusiveGrantRule
var wf_recvmod(C:client)     : bool      # receivemodifiedGrantRule
var wf_grantshared           : bool      # grantsharedRule
var wf_grantexcl             : bool      # grantexclusiveRule
var wf_grantmod              : bool      # grantmodifiedRule

after init {
    s.channel1(C)   := empty1;
    s.channel2_4(C) := empty2_4;
    s.channel3(C)   := empty3;
    s.cache(C)      := invalid;
    s.homeSharerList(C) := false;
    s.homeprobeList(C)  := false;
    s.homeexclusiveGranted := false;
    s.homeCurrentCommand   := empty1;
    s.waiting(C) := false;

    wf_pick(C) := false;
    f_pick(C)  := false;
    wf_sendinv(C)     := false;
    wf_senddown(C)    := false;
    wf_clientinv(C)   := false;
    wf_clientdown(C)  := false;
    wf_recvinvack(C)  := false;
    wf_recvdownack(C) := false;
    wf_recvshared(C)  := false;
    wf_recvexcl(C)    := false;
    wf_recvmod(C)     := false;
    wf_grantshared := false;
    wf_grantexcl   := false;
    wf_grantmod    := false;
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side request generation.  These are *environment* actions: we assume
# no fairness for them, since we never want to force a cache to issue a
# request.  A cache blocks until its previous access has been served.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

action reqsharedRule(cl:client) = {
    require ~s.waiting(cl);
    require s.cache(cl) = invalid & s.channel1(cl) = empty1;
    s.channel1(cl) := reqshared;
    s.waiting(cl) := true;
}

action reqexclusiveRule(cl:client) = {
    require ~s.waiting(cl);
    require (s.cache(cl) = invalid | s.cache(cl) = shared | s.cache(cl) = owned)
            & s.channel1(cl) = empty1;
    s.channel1(cl) := reqexclusive;
    s.waiting(cl) := true;
}

# MESI/MOESI silent upgrade E -> M: no bus traffic, no directory change.
action writeExclusiveRule(cl:client) = {
    require s.cache(cl) = exclusive;
    s.cache(cl) := modified;
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Home directory
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The arbiter of MOESI as literally specified: pick an *arbitrary* client with
# a pending request.  `wf_pick(cl)` is pulsed before the guard (the scheduler
# offered this pick a turn); `f_pick(cl)` is pulsed inside it (the pick
# actually happened) and is the "taken" half of the compassion assumption.
action pickNewRequestRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_pick(cl) := true;
    wf_pick(cl) := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1 & s.channel1(cl) ~= empty1 {
        f_pick(cl) := true;
        f_pick(cl) := false;
        s.homeCurrentCommand := s.channel1(cl);
        s.channel1(cl) := empty1;
        s.homeCurrentclient := cl;
        s.homeprobeList(C) := s.homeSharerList(C);
    }
}

action sendinvalidateRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_sendinv(cl) := true;
    wf_sendinv(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = empty2_4 & s.homeprobeList(cl)
       & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive {
        s.channel2_4(cl) := invalidate;
        s.homeprobeList(cl) := false;
    }
}

action senddowngradeRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_senddown(cl) := true;
    wf_senddown(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = empty2_4 & s.homeprobeList(cl)
       & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared & s.homeexclusiveGranted {
        s.channel2_4(cl) := downgrade;
        s.homeprobeList(cl) := false;
    }
}

action receiveinvalidateAckRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_recvinvack(cl) := true;
    wf_recvinvack(cl) := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & s.channel3(cl) = invalidateAck {
        s.homeSharerList(cl) := false;
        s.homeexclusiveGranted := false;
        s.channel3(cl) := empty3;
    }
}

action receivedowngradeAckRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_recvdownack(cl) := true;
    wf_recvdownack(cl) := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & s.channel3(cl) = downgradeAck {
        s.homeexclusiveGranted := false;
        s.channel3(cl) := empty3;
    }
}

action grantsharedRule = {
    wf_grantshared := true;
    wf_grantshared := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
       & ~s.homeexclusiveGranted
       & (exists I. s.homeSharerList(I))
       & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4 {
        s.homeSharerList(s.homeCurrentclient) := true;
        s.homeCurrentCommand := empty1;
        s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) := grantshared;
    }
}

action grantexclusiveRule = {
    wf_grantexcl := true;
    wf_grantexcl := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
       & (forall I. ~s.homeSharerList(I))
       & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4 {
        s.homeSharerList(s.homeCurrentclient) := true;
        s.homeexclusiveGranted := true;
        s.homeCurrentCommand := empty1;
        s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) := grantexclusive;
        owner := s.homeCurrentclient;
    }
}

action grantmodifiedRule = {
    wf_grantmod := true;
    wf_grantmod := false;
    if s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
       & (forall I. ~s.homeSharerList(I))
       & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4 {
        s.homeSharerList(s.homeCurrentclient) := true;
        s.homeexclusiveGranted := true;
        s.homeCurrentCommand := empty1;
        s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) := grantmodified;
        owner := s.homeCurrentclient;
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side probe handling and grant reception
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

action clientinvalidatesRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_clientinv(cl) := true;
    wf_clientinv(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = invalidate & s.channel3(cl) = empty3 {
        s.channel2_4(cl) := empty2_4;
        s.channel3(cl)   := invalidateAck;
        s.cache(cl)      := invalid;
    }
}

action clientdowngradesRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_clientdown(cl) := true;
    wf_clientdown(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = downgrade & s.channel3(cl) = empty3 {
        s.channel2_4(cl) := empty2_4;
        s.channel3(cl)   := downgradeAck;
        if s.cache(cl) = modified {
            s.cache(cl) := owned;       # MOESI dirty sharing: no writeback
        } else if s.cache(cl) = exclusive {
            s.cache(cl) := shared;
        }
    }
}

action receivesharedGrantRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_recvshared(cl) := true;
    wf_recvshared(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = grantshared {
        s.cache(cl) := shared;
        s.channel2_4(cl) := empty2_4;
        s.waiting(cl) := false;
    }
}

action receiveexclusiveGrantRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_recvexcl(cl) := true;
    wf_recvexcl(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = grantexclusive {
        s.cache(cl) := exclusive;
        s.channel2_4(cl) := empty2_4;
        s.waiting(cl) := false;
    }
}

action receivemodifiedGrantRule(cl:client) = {
    wf_recvmod(cl) := true;
    wf_recvmod(cl) := false;
    if s.channel2_4(cl) = grantmodified {
        s.cache(cl) := modified;
        s.channel2_4(cl) := empty2_4;
        s.waiting(cl) := false;
    }
}

export reqsharedRule
export reqexclusiveRule
export writeExclusiveRule
export pickNewRequestRule
export sendinvalidateRule
export senddowngradeRule
export clientinvalidatesRule
export clientdowngradesRule
export receiveinvalidateAckRule
export receivedowngradeAckRule
export grantsharedRule
export grantexclusiveRule
export grantmodifiedRule
export receivesharedGrantRule
export receiveexclusiveGrantRule
export receivemodifiedGrantRule

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The fairness flags are only momentarily true.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

invariant ~wf_pick(C)
invariant ~f_pick(C)
invariant ~wf_sendinv(C)
invariant ~wf_senddown(C)
invariant ~wf_clientinv(C)
invariant ~wf_clientdown(C)
invariant ~wf_recvinvack(C)
invariant ~wf_recvdownack(C)
invariant ~wf_recvshared(C)
invariant ~wf_recvexcl(C)
invariant ~wf_recvmod(C)
invariant ~wf_grantshared
invariant ~wf_grantexcl
invariant ~wf_grantmod

# ===========================================================================
# SAFETY: the MOESI compatibility table (proved in moesi.ivy; repeated here
# because the liveness argument runs on top of these invariants)
# ===========================================================================

invariant [moesi_M_is_exclusive]
    forall C1, C2. C1 ~= C2 & s.cache(C1) = modified -> s.cache(C2) = invalid

invariant [moesi_E_is_exclusive]
    forall C1, C2. C1 ~= C2 & s.cache(C1) = exclusive -> s.cache(C2) = invalid

invariant [moesi_O_compatible_with_S_only]
    forall C1, C2. C1 ~= C2 & s.cache(C1) = owned
        -> s.cache(C2) = shared | s.cache(C2) = invalid

invariant [moesi_O_is_unique]
    forall C1, C2. s.cache(C1) = owned & s.cache(C2) = owned -> C1 = C2

invariant [excl_unique]
    s.homeexclusiveGranted & s.homeSharerList(C) -> C = owner

invariant [excl_owner_is_sharer]
    s.homeexclusiveGranted -> s.homeSharerList(owner)

invariant [shared_implies_no_writer]
    (s.cache(C) = shared | s.channel2_4(C) = grantshared)
        -> s.homeSharerList(C)
           & (~s.homeexclusiveGranted | s.channel3(C) = downgradeAck)

invariant [writable_is_owner]
    (s.cache(C) = exclusive | s.cache(C) = modified
     | s.channel2_4(C) = grantexclusive | s.channel2_4(C) = grantmodified)
        -> s.homeSharerList(C) & s.homeexclusiveGranted & C = owner

invariant [owned_is_owner]
    s.cache(C) = owned -> s.homeSharerList(C) & C = owner

invariant [owned_not_writable]
    s.cache(C) = owned & s.homeexclusiveGranted -> s.channel3(C) = downgradeAck

invariant [probe_implies_sharer]
    s.homeprobeList(C) -> s.homeSharerList(C)

invariant [invalidate_in_channel]
    s.channel2_4(C) = invalidate
        -> s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
           & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C)

invariant [downgrade_in_channel]
    s.channel2_4(C) = downgrade
        -> s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared & s.homeexclusiveGranted
           & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C) & C = owner

invariant [invalidateAck_in_channel]
    s.channel3(C) = invalidateAck
        -> s.cache(C) = invalid & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
           & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C)

invariant [downgradeAck_in_channel]
    s.channel3(C) = downgradeAck
        -> s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared & s.homeexclusiveGranted
           & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C) & C = owner
           & s.cache(C) ~= exclusive & s.cache(C) ~= modified

invariant [no_overlap]
    s.channel2_4(C) ~= empty2_4 -> s.channel3(C) = empty3

invariant [valid_implies_sharer]
    s.cache(C) ~= invalid -> s.homeSharerList(C)

# ===========================================================================
# Extra invariants needed by the liveness argument
# ===========================================================================

# A waiting client is in exactly one of the three stages.  This is what
# discharges S4 ("something is always scheduled").
invariant [waiting_stages]
    s.waiting(C) <-> (s.channel1(C) ~= empty1
                      | (s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & s.homeCurrentclient = C)
                      | s.channel2_4(C) = grantshared
                      | s.channel2_4(C) = grantexclusive
                      | s.channel2_4(C) = grantmodified)

invariant [stage1_excl]
    s.channel1(C) ~= empty1 ->
        ~(s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & s.homeCurrentclient = C)
        & s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantshared
        & s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantexclusive
        & s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantmodified

invariant [stage2_excl]
    (s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1 & s.homeCurrentclient = C) ->
        s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantshared
        & s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantexclusive
        & s.channel2_4(C) ~= grantmodified

# During a write command, a sharer already taken off the probe list has its
# invalidate (or the ack) in flight: no sharer is ever stuck outside the
# pipeline.  Without this, S4 has a hole.
invariant [inv_in_flight]
    s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
    & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C)
    -> s.channel2_4(C) = invalidate | s.channel3(C) = invalidateAck

# Same for the downgrade pipeline of a read command.
invariant [down_in_flight]
    s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared & s.homeexclusiveGranted
    & s.homeSharerList(C) & ~s.homeprobeList(C)
    -> s.channel2_4(C) = downgrade | s.channel3(C) = downgradeAck


# ===========================================================================
# Fairness assumptions: weak fairness (justice) for every rule.
# ===========================================================================

# Weak fairness for the arbiter is stated for completeness but is NOT used by
# the proof: see [sf_pick] -- weak fairness of the pick is not enough.
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_pick]        forall C. globally eventually wf_pick(C)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Strong fairness (compassion) for the home's request arbiter:
#
#     if C's request is available for picking infinitely often,
#     then the home eventually picks it.
#
# This does not assume the conclusion -- the antecedent still has to be
# discharged, and that is exactly what the pipeline components [05]..[16] do:
# they show the home keeps finishing commands, so C's request keeps becoming
# pickable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
explicit temporal axiom [sf_pick]
  forall C. (globally eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1 & s.channel1(C) ~= empty1))
            -> (globally eventually f_pick(C))
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_sendinv]     forall C. globally eventually wf_sendinv(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_senddown]    forall C. globally eventually wf_senddown(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_clientinv]   forall C. globally eventually wf_clientinv(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_clientdown]  forall C. globally eventually wf_clientdown(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_recvinvack]  forall C. globally eventually wf_recvinvack(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_recvdownack] forall C. globally eventually wf_recvdownack(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_recvshared]  forall C. globally eventually wf_recvshared(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_recvexcl]    forall C. globally eventually wf_recvexcl(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_recvmod]     forall C. globally eventually wf_recvmod(C)
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_grantshared] globally eventually wf_grantshared
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_grantexcl]   globally eventually wf_grantexcl
explicit temporal axiom [wfa_grantmod]    globally eventually wf_grantmod

# ===========================================================================
# THE LIVENESS PROPERTY
# ===========================================================================

explicit temporal property [live]
  forall C. globally (s.waiting(C) -> eventually ~s.waiting(C))
proof {
  tactic skolemizenp;
  instantiate sf_pick with C = _C;
  instantiate wfa_sendinv;
  instantiate wfa_senddown;
  instantiate wfa_clientinv;
  instantiate wfa_clientdown;
  instantiate wfa_recvinvack;
  instantiate wfa_recvdownack;
  instantiate wfa_recvshared;
  instantiate wfa_recvexcl;
  instantiate wfa_recvmod;
  instantiate wfa_grantshared;
  instantiate wfa_grantexcl;
  instantiate wfa_grantmod;
  tactic ranking with {

    # ===== stage 1 ========================================================
    #
    # Abbreviate the compassion antecedent
    #
    #     E  =  homeCurrentCommand = empty1 & channel1(_C) ~= empty1
    #
    # Following McMillan's `strongfair.ivy` idiom, the symbolic tableau for E
    # splits stage 1 into three cases:
    #   * E holds infinitely often               -> [01], compassion delivers
    #                                               the pick
    #   * E holds finitely often, last E not yet -> [00], the tableau bit
    #                                               itself is the ranking and
    #                                               must drop to false
    #   * E never happens again                  -> the home is never idle
    #                                               again, so the pipeline
    #                                               [05]..[16] is required, and
    #                                               it drives the home to a
    #                                               grant -- which makes it
    #                                               idle.  Contradiction.

    # [00] E happens only finitely often, but the last E has not happened yet.
    definition work_created[00](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[00](N:client)  = eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                                        & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1)
    definition work_invar[00]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[00](N:client)= ~(eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                                          & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1))
    definition work_helpful[00](N:client) = ~(globally eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                                                   & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1))
                                            & (eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                                           & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1))

    # [01] E happens infinitely often, so by compassion the home eventually
    # picks _C's request and empties channel1(_C).
    definition work_created[01](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[01](N:client)  = s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1
    definition work_invar[01]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[01](N:client)= f_pick(_C)
    definition work_helpful[01](N:client) = (globally eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                                                  & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1))
                                            & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1

    # ===== stage 3: _C consumes its grant =================================
    definition work_created[02](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[02](N:client)  = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_invar[02]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[02](N:client)= wf_recvshared(N)
    definition work_helpful[02](N:client) = N = _C & s.channel2_4(_C) = grantshared

    definition work_created[03](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[03](N:client)  = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_invar[03]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[03](N:client)= wf_recvexcl(N)
    definition work_helpful[03](N:client) = N = _C & s.channel2_4(_C) = grantexclusive

    definition work_created[04](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[04](N:client)  = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_invar[04]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[04](N:client)= wf_recvmod(N)
    definition work_helpful[04](N:client) = N = _C & s.channel2_4(_C) = grantmodified

    # ===== stage 2a: the invalidation pipeline (write requests) ===========
    #
    #   sharer --sendinvalidate--> invalidate in ch2_4
    #          --clientinvalidates--> invalidateAck in ch3
    #          --receiveinvalidateAck--> off the sharer list
    #
    # Each ranking is a superset of the stages still to come, so the rule
    # that advances a client conserves it.

    definition work_created[05](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[05](N:client)  = s.homeSharerList(N)
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
    definition work_invar[05]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[05](N:client)= wf_recvinvack(N)
    definition work_helpful[05](N:client) = s.channel3(N) = invalidateAck

    definition work_created[06](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[06](N:client)  = s.homeSharerList(N)
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
                                            & s.channel3(N) ~= invalidateAck
    definition work_invar[06]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[06](N:client)= wf_clientinv(N)
    definition work_helpful[06](N:client) = s.channel2_4(N) = invalidate

    definition work_created[07](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[07](N:client)  = s.homeSharerList(N)
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
                                            & s.channel3(N) ~= invalidateAck
                                            & s.channel2_4(N) ~= invalidate
    definition work_invar[07]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[07](N:client)= wf_sendinv(N)
    definition work_helpful[07](N:client) = s.homeprobeList(N)
                                            & s.channel2_4(N) = empty2_4
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive

    # ===== stage 2b: the downgrade pipeline (read requests) ===============
    #
    # This is the MOESI-specific half.  A read request that finds the line
    # writable somewhere does not invalidate it -- it downgrades the owner
    # (M -> O, or E -> S) and the owner keeps the data.  The ranking is
    # "write permission is still outstanding for this read command"; it is
    # the same three-stage shape as above.

    definition work_created[08](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[08](N:client)  = s.homeexclusiveGranted
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
    definition work_invar[08]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[08](N:client)= wf_recvdownack(N)
    definition work_helpful[08](N:client) = s.channel3(N) = downgradeAck

    definition work_created[09](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[09](N:client)  = s.homeexclusiveGranted
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                            & s.channel3(N) ~= downgradeAck
    definition work_invar[09]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[09](N:client)= wf_clientdown(N)
    definition work_helpful[09](N:client) = s.channel2_4(N) = downgrade

    definition work_created[10](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[10](N:client)  = s.homeexclusiveGranted
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                            & s.channel3(N) ~= downgradeAck
                                            & s.channel2_4(N) ~= downgrade
    definition work_invar[10]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[10](N:client)= wf_senddown(N)
    definition work_helpful[10](N:client) = s.homeprobeList(N)
                                            & s.channel2_4(N) = empty2_4
                                            & s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                            & s.homeexclusiveGranted

    # ===== stage 2c: drain a stale grant that blocks a probe ==============
    #
    # A client that has not yet consumed its own grant occupies channel2_4,
    # which blocks the probe the home needs to send it.  Draining it is a
    # genuine pipeline stage.

    definition work_created[11](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[11](N:client)  = s.channel2_4(N) = grantshared
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))
    definition work_invar[11]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[11](N:client)= wf_recvshared(N)
    definition work_helpful[11](N:client) = s.channel2_4(N) = grantshared
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))

    definition work_created[12](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[12](N:client)  = s.channel2_4(N) = grantexclusive
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))
    definition work_invar[12]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[12](N:client)= wf_recvexcl(N)
    definition work_helpful[12](N:client) = s.channel2_4(N) = grantexclusive
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))

    definition work_created[13](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[13](N:client)  = s.channel2_4(N) = grantmodified
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))
    definition work_invar[13]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[13](N:client)= wf_recvmod(N)
    definition work_helpful[13](N:client) = s.channel2_4(N) = grantmodified
                                            & (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                               | (s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                                  & s.homeexclusiveGranted))

    # ===== stage 2d: the home issues the grant, ending the command ========

    definition work_created[14](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[14](N:client)  = s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
    definition work_invar[14]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[14](N:client)= wf_grantshared
    definition work_helpful[14](N:client) = s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                            & ~s.homeexclusiveGranted
                                            & (exists I. s.homeSharerList(I))
                                            & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4

    definition work_created[15](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[15](N:client)  = s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
    definition work_invar[15]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[15](N:client)= wf_grantexcl
    definition work_helpful[15](N:client) = s.homeCurrentCommand = reqshared
                                            & (forall I. ~s.homeSharerList(I))
                                            & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4

    definition work_created[16](N:client) = true
    definition work_needed[16](N:client)  = s.homeCurrentCommand ~= empty1
    definition work_invar[16]             = s.waiting(_C)
    definition work_progress[16](N:client)= wf_grantmod
    definition work_helpful[16](N:client) = s.homeCurrentCommand = reqexclusive
                                            & (forall I. ~s.homeSharerList(I))
                                            & s.channel2_4(s.homeCurrentclient) = empty2_4

    # The compassion assumption, re-stated as a state invariant of the
    # tableau.  `instantiate sf_pick` only pins it at the initial state, but
    # `l2s_progress_eventually[01]` is a postcondition checked at every state.
    # The lift is sound because []<>p is insensitive to finite prefixes, and it
    # is inductive from the local tableau constraints -- Ivy proves it, you
    # just have to ask.  (Same line as in McMillan's `strongfair.ivy`.)
    invariant (globally eventually (s.homeCurrentCommand = empty1
                                    & s.channel1(_C) ~= empty1))
              -> (globally eventually f_pick(_C))
  }
}
